# Lanes on which the engine at the reference commit differs between an edit history and a cold
# layout of the same input. One lane prefix per line, then the finding. The oracle counts and
# reports every hit; a lane leaves this list when the engine is fixed.

# Scripted steps that differ from cold: `step <case> <NN>`, then the finding.

# Requests of the seeded driver that differ from a cold layout of the same input, found at the
# reference commit with the full tier (seeds 1-4, 60 requests):
# `seed <case> <seed> <step> <first differing lane> | <what the request did>`.
# Every one reproduces as a single request after a cold layout. Replay one with
# `layout-oracle fuzz --case <case> --seed <seed> --steps <step + 1>`. The driver continues past
# each from a cold layout, so the entries of one run do not depend on each other being fixed.
